content.text:
Now add responsive rules. Existing @media max-height 560 and 420. Need add for new screens. We can append inside existing blocks or add new media queries after current responsive section. Let's insert near `@media (max-height: 560px)` adding rules, and 420. Use edit.

At max-height 560, we want:
```
.hub-wrap, .map-wrap, .hangar-wrap { padding: 1vh 0; }
.hub-head { padding-bottom:6px; }
.hub-intro { margin:7px 0; }
.hub-intro h2 { font-size:clamp(23px,3vw,32px);}
.hub-intro p { font-size:8.5px; margin-top:4px;}
.hub-card { min-height: 106px; padding:9px 11px;}
.hub-card-title {font-size:clamp(18px,2.2vw,24px);}
.hub-card-desc {font-size:7.5px; max-width:68%;}
.hub-card-icon { width:48px;height:48px;}
.hub-head-right {font-size:6px; gap:10px;}
.menu-head {padding-bottom:6px;}
.menu-heading h1 {font-size:clamp(20px,2.6vw,30px);}
.map-art {height:clamp(52px,14vh,82px);}
.map-info {padding:6px 8px 7px;}
.map-desc {font-size:7px;}
.map-grid {margin:7px 0;}
.map-foot {font-size:5.5px;}
.hangar-lead {margin:7px 0; padding:7px 10px;}
.hangar-lead p {font-size:8px;}
.hangar-stamp {font-size:9px; padding:3px 6px;}
.hangar-roster {gap:6px;}
.hangar-card {padding:6px 4px;}
.hangar-card-icon {width:29px;height:29px;}
.hangar-card-icon svg {width:24px;height:24px;}
.hangar-foot {margin-top:7px;}
.hangar-foot .deploy-btn {padding:6px 14px 5px;}
.hangar-foot .deploy-btn span {font-size:12px;}
.hangar-foot .deploy-btn small {display:none;}
```
At max-height 420, maybe hub: hide desc and icon? Let's see. 844x390 already under 420. Our 560 sizes should fit. 390 height with hub: 6px header top? `.hub-wrap padding 1vh` = 3.9. header height ~31, intro margin 7+ h2 32+ eyebrow 7+ p 12 = 58, cards 106, footer margin 7 + 10, gaps = 31+7+... total maybe 3.9*2+31+58+106+17=220, fits. Plenty. Could enlarge cards at 390. But okay.

Map: header ~40 + grid margin 14 + art 55 + info ~90 = 145 + foot 12 = 211. Fits.

Hangar ~ header40 + lead 40 + roster 80 + foot 30 = 190. Good.

At max-height 360 maybe cards tight; add rules:
```
@media (max-height:360px) {
 .hub-card-desc, .map-desc, .hangar-lead p { display:none; }
 .hub-card {min-height:88px;}
 .map-art {height:44px;}
 .map-info {gap:2px;}
 .hangar-card em {display:none;}
}
```
Fine.

At max-width maybe title screen h1 and start-wrap currently at 844. We'll test and adjust.

Also `.start-wrap` width and margin might conflict with new space. Keep.

Portrait screens: `.screen` hidden on portrait for start/end only via CSS line 1278: `.start-screen, .end-screen { display:none; }`. New menu screens would remain visible in portrait but rotate screen overlays at z300. Since rotateScreen displays and covers, okay. But `.rotate-screen` display none default, and media portrait sets `display:flex`; other screens still under it. Fine.

Add responsive rules.

